WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.233 --> 00:00:03.369
 Ted, Deker, congratulations.

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:07.540
Your work has secured your place
in the "Forged in Fire" final.

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:09.775
When you arrived here,
you forged a signature

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:11.878
blade of your own design.

00:00:11.944 --> 00:00:13.612
Now we're sending
you home to forge

00:00:13.712 --> 00:00:15.615
an iconic weapon from history--

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:20.486
the tabar.

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:23.423
 It's not a sword.

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:25.558
 The tabar is a
battle ax originating

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:30.296
from Persia, Armenia, India,
and surrounding cultures.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:34.266
Usually made entirely of metal,
it has a strongly curved blade

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:36.536
and a hammerhead
pole that was often

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:38.604
decorated with inscriptions.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:41.307
The light metallic handle
is what makes the ax

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:44.077
unique and durable in battle.

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:46.312
During the 17th
and 18th centuries,

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.781
the tabar was a standard
weapon of the mountain

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:53.386
warriors of India, Afghanistan,
and what is now Pakistan.

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:56.355
With its double edged
blade and piercing spike,

00:00:56.455 --> 00:00:59.391
it was an unrelenting
weapon of war.

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:03.162
This fierce weapon is featured
in the iconic film series

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.097
"The Lord of the Rings."

00:01:05.197 --> 00:01:06.699
You will have five
days at your home

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:08.735
forge to complete your work.

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:09.836
At the end of five
days, you will

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:13.239
return and present your
tabar to our panel of judges.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:16.075
Only after they've submitted
those weapons to a series

00:01:16.141 --> 00:01:19.012
of brutal and dynamic
tests will they

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:21.247
declare one of you the
"Forged in Fire" champion

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:24.817
and the recipient
of a $10,000 check.

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:26.085
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:26.185 --> 00:01:27.420
We'll see you in five days.

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.725
 My name is Ted Thompson.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:36.028 line:8%
I split my time between
knife making and tattooing.

00:01:36.128 --> 00:01:37.563
Been a knife fanatic
my whole life,

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:41.901
and I just started
blacksmithing to see if I could.

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.569
Today, I'm going to
work on the handle.

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:46.372
There's a lot to think
about on getting everything

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:48.575
put together the right way.

00:01:54.713 --> 00:01:57.584
Right now it's just a really,
really long eye poker.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:02.588
I decided to make an
asset out of an eight

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:03.590
pound sledgehammer head.

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:06.592
It's a very good,
high impact steel.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.694
I want to be able to chop a
car in half with this thing.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:16.535
So-- I'm going to do an
asymmetrical double headed.

00:02:16.635 --> 00:02:21.074
One blade's going to be a little
bit heavier than the other.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:23.209
I'm [inaudible] the
metal so it spread

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.912
wide so I can start building
the beards of the blade.

00:02:37.656 --> 00:02:38.157
Awesome.

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:39.526
Cool profile too.

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:47.800
I don't have a forge big enough
to fit the ax fully assembled.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:52.471
So I used the front of the
forge and my cutting torch

00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:54.207
and got it up to
critical [inaudible]..

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:58.178
And I quenched one side
and then the other.

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.583
Sweet.

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:06.018
Yep, she's hard.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:07.287
It'll be ready to go.

00:03:11.657 --> 00:03:12.591
 I'm Deker.

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:15.394 line:8%
I work as a computer
security consultant.

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:17.597 line:8%
Blacksmithing and knife
making is sort of a sideline

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:19.999
that I do as a little
bit of therapy.

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:22.202
Planning on doing some pattern
rolling for this project.

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:24.470 line:8%
If it's worth making, it's
worth making in Damascus.

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:26.673 line:8%
This piece here is going
to turn into a long bar

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:28.440 line:14%
of steel similar to this.

00:03:28.507 --> 00:03:30.476
That'll then get
cut up into sections

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:33.880
so I can stack multiple layers
together in a billet to weld.

00:03:36.548 --> 00:03:40.085
Time to get this steel starting
to look less like a lump

00:03:40.185 --> 00:03:41.754
of stuff and more like an ax.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.589
Inside the mind of a madman.

00:03:43.655 --> 00:03:45.991
I'm going into the press to
do the very first [inaudible]

00:03:46.058 --> 00:03:46.892
operation.

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:47.994
Defining moment.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:48.895
I start to squish.

00:03:53.899 --> 00:03:57.670
And just that right there
probably saved me 45 minutes.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.640
Definitely a little
more sexy than what

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.242
I left with yesterday.

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.479
Now I've got the
spike in the forge.

00:04:06.545 --> 00:04:07.914
I've got to get that drawn out.

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:11.517
Good gravy.

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:14.620
This spike is going to
make us heavier than hell.

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:17.457
I'm behind what I had set
myself for a schedule.

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:19.158
I've got a lot to
figure out, and I've

00:04:19.224 --> 00:04:20.492
still got a lot to do tomorrow.

00:04:20.559 --> 00:04:22.295
I certainly hope
nothing goes wrong,

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:24.264
but failure is not an option.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:37.943
 Let's go kill something.

00:04:38.043 --> 00:04:38.811
Sweet.

00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:44.017
 That's done.

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:47.052
Come hell or high
water, that's it.

00:04:47.152 --> 00:04:49.222
 Bladesmiths, this
is the kill test.

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:51.457
The tabar's three
sharp sides allows

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:53.826
for three times the chances
of killing an opponent

00:04:53.926 --> 00:04:54.860
in the heat of battle.

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:57.596
To test the lethality and
function of your weapon,

00:04:57.696 --> 00:04:59.832
I will test all three
sides by chopping

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:01.867
at this animal carcass.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:02.602
Ted, you're up.

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:03.135
Are you ready.

00:05:03.235 --> 00:05:03.969
 Heck yeah.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:04.971
Let's do this.

00:05:23.622 --> 00:05:26.292
 Well, Ted, the
design of your blade

00:05:26.358 --> 00:05:29.361
really digs into the carcass.

00:05:29.461 --> 00:05:31.764
The hooks grabs
everything that's in there

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:34.100
and rips it right out.

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.302
Balance is a little
bit heavy, but it

00:05:36.368 --> 00:05:38.370
will do a lot of destruction.

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:41.307
This weapon, sir, will kill.

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:42.007
 Awesome.

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:43.175
 Good job, sir.

00:05:43.275 --> 00:05:44.042
 Thank you.

00:05:44.109 --> 00:05:45.244
 Deker, it's your turn.

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:46.144
You ready?

00:05:46.211 --> 00:05:47.713
 Let's cut some bacon, Doug.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:48.614
 Let's do this.

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:08.734
 Yes.

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:09.768
Yes.

00:06:09.835 --> 00:06:11.236
Yes.

00:06:11.303 --> 00:06:14.640
 Well, Deker, your
edges are very sharp.

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:16.275
As you can see what it
did, it pretty much went

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:17.877
to cut all the way through.

00:06:17.943 --> 00:06:22.447
The feel, though, is a little
bit rounded for the handle.

00:06:22.514 --> 00:06:25.317
But nonetheless, it's light.

00:06:25.417 --> 00:06:28.654
So I can generate more
power to control it.

00:06:28.754 --> 00:06:32.291
This is a weapon that will kill.

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:33.325
Good job, sir.

00:06:33.392 --> 00:06:34.660
 Thank you.

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:37.530
 I'm going to pass things
off to Dave for the next test.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:38.965
 All right, gentlemen.

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:40.700
It's time for the strength test.

00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:41.800
Ted, you're up.

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:42.668
Are you ready?

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:43.168
 I'm ready.

00:06:43.268 --> 00:06:45.571
 All right.

00:06:45.637 --> 00:06:50.610
 All right, 3, 2, 1, engaging.

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:03.523
You put a really good
crease in the shield,

00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:07.860
and that's a heck of a chop
you just chopped in in hardened

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:09.895
oak of this barrel.

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:13.132
A little bit of a roll
right up here on this edge

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:15.067
that hit the shield.

00:07:15.168 --> 00:07:18.004
And the shaft of the ax
looks perfectly straight.

00:07:18.104 --> 00:07:19.738
Didn't flex at all.

00:07:19.805 --> 00:07:20.706
Well done.

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:22.074
 Thank you.

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:23.342
 All right, Deker.

00:07:23.409 --> 00:07:24.944
You're up.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:25.845
 Let's tap a keg.

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:33.186
 All right, 3, 2, 1, engage.

00:07:42.094 --> 00:07:44.663
 Son of a bitch.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:47.500
 Well, Deker,
your spike sheared

00:07:47.566 --> 00:07:49.768
off right at that rivet point.

00:07:49.835 --> 00:07:51.370
 Yep.

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:54.573
 You put a good
crease in the shield.

00:07:54.673 --> 00:07:56.542
[inaudible] you put a
good cut in the barrel.

00:07:58.777 --> 00:08:01.214
The edge of the ax here
that hit the barrel,

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:05.117
you just see a little
coloration, some shiny spots.

00:08:05.183 --> 00:08:08.887
The side that hit the shield,
doesn't look like any damage

00:08:08.987 --> 00:08:10.389
at all.

00:08:10.489 --> 00:08:13.191
But that spike coming off--

00:08:13.258 --> 00:08:16.762
well, that's a problem.

00:08:16.828 --> 00:08:22.602
 At the moment when that
spike fell, my heart just sank.

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:25.571
 Gentlemen, you both put in
a lot of work on your tabars.

00:08:25.638 --> 00:08:28.006
But in this arena, there can
only be one "Forged in Fire"

00:08:28.073 --> 00:08:28.774
champion.

00:08:32.378 --> 00:08:36.581
Ted, you are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:08:36.648 --> 00:08:39.117
Deker, your weapon
did not make the cut.

00:08:39.217 --> 00:08:39.918
 Congratulations.

00:08:39.985 --> 00:08:40.485
 [inaudible]

00:08:40.552 --> 00:08:41.553
 Ted, congratulations.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.022
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:08:43.088 --> 00:08:45.290
and will be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:08:45.357 --> 00:08:46.058
Good job.

00:08:46.158 --> 00:08:46.792
 Awesome.

00:08:46.892 --> 00:08:47.693
Thank you.

00:08:47.793 --> 00:08:50.162
I joined this
competition to see if I

00:08:50.262 --> 00:08:51.630
had what it took
to make a better

00:08:51.696 --> 00:08:53.198
weapon than three other guys.

00:08:53.299 --> 00:08:54.099
And I did it.

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:55.401
And that makes me happy.

00:08:55.467 --> 00:08:57.036
 Props for putting
"Forged in Fire--"

00:08:57.136 --> 00:08:58.136
- Yeah.
- --on your blade.

00:08:58.203 --> 00:09:01.072
 And Persian around here
says "caution-- sharp edge."

00:09:01.139 --> 00:09:02.208
 Nice touch.

00:09:02.274 --> 00:09:04.943
 When I'm working with a
bunch of guys I really respect,

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:07.346
they're going to push
the quality that I do.

00:09:07.413 --> 00:09:08.447
It pushed me a lot.

00:09:08.513 --> 00:09:12.018
That's what I enjoyed about it.

